{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nJira DC summary updates can retry in both pycontribs/Jira and `_with_connection_retry`. The selected route needs a dedicated no-SDK-retry client and per-call wrapper policy without changing legacy callers.\n\n## Outcome\nImplement the DC summary executor with a guarded `max_retries=0` client and fixed GET -> PUT -> GET invocation. Ambiguous PUT recovery uses a separate single-attempt GET under the shared budget.\n\n## Plan\n1. Construct a dedicated executor client through the pinned public `jira.JIRA(..., max_retries=0)` argument; fail fast unless `_session.max_retries == 0`. Preserve legacy client construction.\n2. Add an injected one-attempt/no-sleep policy to `_with_connection_retry` for selected executor calls; preserve legacy wrapper defaults.\n3. Make one write invocation issue exactly GET/PUT/GET. Failure ends the invocation; successful read-back is authoritative.\n4. After ambiguous PUT, consume another physical invocation for one GET observation. Desired state recovers, conclusive old state may replay within budget, and failed/inconclusive observation returns `commit_unknown`.\n5. Return classification/delay metadata to the shared owner; do not sleep or replay in SDK/adapter layers.\n6. Emit exactly one redacted completion log for every DC terminal/exhausted outcome or cleanup failure. Include only logical id, disposition, invocation count, request count, cleanup status, `retry_not_before`, and one redacted message capped at 512 Unicode code points; cap the whole serialized log at 1,024 Unicode code points.\n\n## Testing\nUse fake sessions with raw request counters and poison sleepers/retry adapters. Include the proven Jira 3.10.5 constructor/session guard plus completion-log field, cardinality, redaction, and size assertions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The dedicated executor client passes `max_retries=0` and rejects a nonzero session value.\n- [ ] Legacy DC client SDK retry remains unchanged.\n- [ ] Each selected write invocation is exactly GET/PUT/GET without hidden repeats.\n- [ ] Selected wrapper calls perform one attempt and no sleep, while legacy wrapper behavior remains unchanged.\n- [ ] Desired observation recovers without another write.\n- [ ] Conclusive old state permits only remaining-budget replay.\n- [ ] Failed or inconclusive observation returns non-replaying `commit_unknown`.\n- [ ] Every DC terminal/exhausted outcome or cleanup failure emits exactly one completion log with only logical id, disposition, invocation/request counts, cleanup status, `retry_not_before`, and one redacted message capped at 512 Unicode code points; the whole log is at most 1,024 Unicode code points.\n\n## Out of scope\nCore dispatch/handler integration and other DC operation families."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787032870309887001,"uuid":"f66c4b26-b0f1-415d-8780-4dd54e4e9dfe"}